## README

# @authority-os/sdk

TypeScript SDK for [Authority OS](https://github.com/IsaiahDupree/authority-os) - Multi-tenant entity visibility operating system for agencies.

## Features

- ✅ **Full TypeScript support** with type inference from Zod schemas
- ✅ **Async/await interface** for all API operations
- ✅ **Auto-pagination** with AsyncGenerator support
- ✅ **Streaming** support for real-time audit progress and content generation
- ✅ **Retry logic** with exponential backoff for network errors and rate limits
- ✅ **Comprehensive error handling** with typed error classes
- ✅ **MCP integration** for AI agents (Model Context Protocol)
- ✅ **Browser and Node.js** compatible
- ✅ **Tree-shakeable** ESM and CJS builds
- ✅ **80%+ test coverage** with Vitest

## Installation

```bash
npm install @authority-os/sdk
```

## Quick Start

```typescript
import { AuthorityOS } from '@authority-os/sdk';

const client = new AuthorityOS({
  apiKey: process.env.AOS_API_KEY!,
  baseUrl: 'http://localhost:3000', // or your production URL
});

// List entities
const entities = await client.entities.list({ page: 1, perPage: 10 });

// Create an entity
const entity = await client.entities.create({
  name: 'Example Company',
  website: 'https://example.com',
  industry: 'Technology',
});

// Trigger an audit
const audit = await client.audits.trigger(entity.id);

// Wait for completion
const result = await client.audits.wait(audit.id);
console.log('Audit score:', result.overall_score);

// Get recommendations
const recs = await client.recommendations.list(entity.id, {
  priority: 'high',
});

// Clean up
client.close();
```

## API Reference

### Client Initialization

```typescript
const client = new AuthorityOS({
  apiKey: string;           // Required: Your API key
  baseUrl?: string;         // Optional: API base URL (default: http://localhost:3000)
  timeout?: number;         // Optional: Request timeout in ms (default: 30000)
  fetch?: typeof fetch;     // Optional: Custom fetch implementation
  requestInterceptors?: RequestInterceptor[];  // Optional: Request middleware
  responseInterceptors?: ResponseInterceptor[]; // Optional: Response middleware
});
```

### Resources

#### Entities

```typescript
// List entities with pagination
await client.entities.list({ page: 1, perPage: 10, search: 'query' });

// Auto-paginate through all entities
for await (const entity of client.entities.listAll({ search: 'query' })) {
  console.log(entity.name);
}

// Get a specific entity
await client.entities.get(entityId);

// Create an entity
await client.entities.create({ name, website, industry, description });

// Update an entity
await client.entities.update(entityId, { name, industry });

// Delete an entity
await client.entities.delete(entityId);
```

#### Audits

```typescript
// Trigger an audit
await client.audits.trigger(entityId, 'full');

// Get audit status
await client.audits.get(auditId);

// Wait for audit to complete
await client.audits.wait(auditId, {
  timeoutMs: 60000,
  pollIntervalMs: 2000,
});

// List audits for an entity
await client.audits.list(entityId, { page: 1, perPage: 10 });
```

#### Recommendations

```typescript
// List recommendations
await client.recommendations.list(entityId, {
  status: 'pending',
  priority: 'high',
});

// Mark as complete
await client.recommendations.complete(recommendationId);

// Dismiss a recommendation
await client.recommendations.dismiss(recommendationId);
```

#### Agent (AI Features)

```typescript
// Get agent context for an entity
const context = await client.agent.getContext(entityId);

// Search across entities, recommendations, and content
const results = await client.agent.search('query', ['entities', 'content']);

// Stream audit progress
for await (const event of client.agent.streamAudit(auditId)) {
  console.log(event.type, event.data);
}

// Batch context retrieval
const contexts = await client.agent.batchContext([id1, id2, id3]);
```

